# Normalise line endings to LF, in the repository and in the working tree.
#
# Prettier's default is `endOfLine: lf`, and there is no prettier config file
# here overriding it. On Windows `core.autocrlf=true` checks everything out as
# CRLF, so every single line becomes a `prettier/prettier` violation: the lint
# script reports tens of thousands of them, and — because `pnpm run lint` passes
# `--fix` — running it rewrites the entire tree's line endings.
#
# Declaring `eol=lf` here makes the working tree LF on every platform, which is
# what prettier and the CI checkout already expect. Files already checked out as
# CRLF keep those endings until they are checked out again; run
# `git rm --cached -r . && git reset --hard` (or re-clone) to normalise an
# existing working copy.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Keep these byte-for-byte.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
